 to scale across DACH.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sales cycle ownership</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Co-plan and execute discovery calls to understand customer requirements, their technical environment and current business challenges.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and deliver compelling demonstrations that solve customer problems, quantify the value of solving those problems, and tell a clear, credible story of how Synthesia solves them better than anything else.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understand and overcome technical objections and integration concerns; identify blockers early and develop solution paths with customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support stakeholder workshops that connect Synthesia to the buyer’s broader technology strategy on complex, multi-stakeholder deals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Account Executives to define account and deal strategy, advise on competitive positioning, assess opportunity stage, and forecast your book of business for leadership.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Demo excellence</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and execute repeatable demo methodologies that prove Synthesia’s business value quickly, whether the customer is deploying Studio at scale, designing Roleplay Sessions for skill uplift, or integrating Interactive Avatars into their product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify, build relationships with, and actively empower executive champions within customer organizations so they can advocate for Synthesia internally.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and maintain reusable assets across demo environments, use cases, integration templates, objections and industry playbooks, brought to life directly in Synthesia’s platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support POC and pilot readouts as a business narrative, not a feature tour, learning to bring storytelling and executive presence to the room as you grow into more senior conversations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide technical guidance on platform capabilities, API and SDK integrations, security, compliance topics (SOC 2, GDPR, enterprise identity) and scalability for global deployments.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product and industry expertise</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain deep expertise on Synthesia’s platform capabilities across all product lines, roadmap and positioning to highlight value-driving use cases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop deep vertical knowledge, establishing yourself as a subject matter expert and building trust with executive buyers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay ahead of the AI-native learning and enablement space, so you can credibly discuss how customers are shifting from current, static methods to interactive practice and measurable skill development.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ecosystem collaboration</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product: share customer and prospect product and competitive feedback with pre-sales leadership and Product, flagging pain points, missing capabilities and gaps that surface in your deals to help shape the roadmap.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product Marketing: work with Product Marketing to understand and apply messaging and positioning in your deal cycles, and contribute to reusable assets like demo scripts and competitive battlecards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customer Success: brief Customer Success on technical context and champion relationships at handover, so your POCs and pilots convert cleanly into production deployments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enablement: review and enhance enablement content based on what works best in preparing team members for client engagements, and deliver and evaluate certification as needed to accelerate understanding in the commercial team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of pre-sales, solutions engineering or customer-facing technical experience at SaaS companies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong consultative discovery, stakeholder management and communication skills, with the ability to engage credibly with both executive decision-makers (CHRO, CLO, Head of L&amp;D, CTO) and technical audiences (IT, security, developers).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical depth in at least one area (creation flows, APIs, integrations such as LMS, HCM, CRM and identity, security, or compliance) and a willingness to learn quickly across domains.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency with sales methodologies such as MEDDPICC and Command of the Message, and comfort translating technical requirements into business value and ROI conversations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A problem-solving approach built on gathering requirements, asking clarifying questions and adapting solutions to customer needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent business and technical presentation skills, in person and remote, and the ability to explain complex AI and integration concepts clearly to both technical and non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Self-motivated and organized, with the ability to manage multiple POCs, demos and customer conversations simultaneously while meeting deadlines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative mindset; you thrive working with AEs, Product, Customer Success and other teams to drive customer and company success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product orientation and genuine curiosity about how customers use technology.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness to travel to visit key customers for discovery, executive conversations and on-site demos.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We’d be particularly excited if</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can also speak Spanish and/or Italian.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re based in Munich, Berlin, Zurich or London, so you can spend time in our offices. This is a hybrid role, with 2+ days a week in the office.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compensation</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a competitive salary, equity and benefits. Your offer will reflect your experience, skills and the scope of the role.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/synthesia/senior-solutions-engineer-german-speaker-germany-322058","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Germany","created_at":1794087614},{"slug":"account-executive-enterprise-dach-germany-52771","company_name":"Redis","title":"Account Executive (Enterprise), DACH","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who we are</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're Redis. We built the product that runs the fast apps our world runs on. (If you checked the weather, used your credit card, or looked at your flight status online today, you’re welcome.) At Redis, you’ll work with the fastest, simplest technology in the business—whether you’re building it, telling its story, or selling it to our 10,000+ worldwide customers. We’re creating a faster world with simpler experiences. You in?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our ideal candidate is a collaborative individual with an entrepreneurial mindset who thrives in a fast-paced environment and yearns to join a hyper-growth company where you can make a real difference. Your portfolio will include leading brands in your territory that are ready to execute on an enterprise-grade Redis deployment. It’s hard work but incredibly rewarding and a lot of fun! We also recognize that you do have a life and at Redis we go to great lengths to ensure the wellbeing of all our employees is at the heart of everything that we do.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you are a new business hunter with a passion for scaling a business and owning your own territory, then we would like to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Why join Redis now</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Redis is one of the world’s most successful Open Source Software projects with widespread adoption in the industry</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Redis is on a pathway to IPO</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commission is uncapped with accelerators</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Best in breed Sales training in MEDDIC, and our comprehensive Sales Enablement programs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stock option grants on joining</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What you’ll do:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Formulate and execute a sales strategy plan to drive revenue growth for your territory.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify, qualify and develop sales pipeline collaborating with internal teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Close business to exceed monthly, quarterly and annual quota objectives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build strong and effective relationships with your customers, delivering the value they come to expect from you and from Redis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work independently and with the whole team, up-selling and cross-selling.<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">What will you need to have?</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5e