trong>Handle medicines safely</strong>: Use designated holding areas, never leave medicines unattended in walkways or packing areas, and immediately quarantine damaged or suspect stock for Shift Lead review.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Keep the floor safe and ready</strong>: Clear cardboard, keep stations tidy and exits unobstructed, remove immediate hazards and report concerns promptly. Operate equipment only within your training and authorisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work as one team</strong>: Support fellow Warehouse Operatives, cover neighbouring areas during breaks and promptly flag stock discrepancies or rotation errors.</p></li></ul><h2>Need to have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Warehouse knowledge</strong>: You understand warehouse operations, stock control, Health &amp; Safety and GDP requirements, and put them into practice.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Attention to detail</strong>: You check medication strengths, order matches and storage conditions carefully. Accuracy is essential.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership</strong>: You stay organised, anticipate what's needed and manage your area independently as priorities change.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Teamwork</strong>: You communicate clearly, flag issues early and bring reliable, consistent effort to every shift.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A hands-on approach</strong>: You can fulfil the role's physical duties, including continuous on-foot activity and routine manual handling.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Regulated operations</strong>: You've worked in regulated warehousing, logistics, pharmacy or healthcare.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cold-chain knowledge</strong>: You understand how to handle temperature-controlled medicines and protect them throughout the packing process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Warehouse systems</strong>: You've used warehouse management tools to track stock and identify discrepancies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equipment qualifications</strong>: You hold forklift or pump truck certification, or baler sign-off. If you don't, we'll provide training.</p></li></ul><h2>Our cultural standards</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We aim to make this your life's work. This should be the most challenging, most rewarding role of your life. Accordingly, these are the core cultural standards to which we hold ourselves &amp; our team-members:</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Belief in the mission</strong>: We will have served 100 million patients by the end of 2035 and we transform the life of most patients who join. We have a lot of work to do. We are obsessed with our patients and are dedicated to the mission.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Unwavering integrity</strong>: We are at the frontier, so we often live in ambiguity with no trodden path. When we can't look to others for guidance, we must maintain impeccable ethics and unwavering integrity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Only the paranoid survive</strong>: Bad sh*t is coming. By joining us, you're choosing to sail straight towards the storms with unhesitating conviction. However much we've already done, however far we've already come — it's still Day 1 and all our work is ahead of us.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>If we're average we fail</strong>: We are only interested in "insanely great", a focus on the quality of our execution that in everyday life would be considered pathological. We have a dedication to excellence and reject incompetence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commitment to candor</strong>: That which can be destroyed by the truth should be. You get full transparency from the company and the company expects full transparency from you. We never say anything about someone that we wouldn't say to them directly. We give feedback with love and do not need to protect people from fleeting physical sensations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A maniacal sense of urgency</strong>: We execute at an intensity that most people think is impossible. Speed is critical and we need things done yesterday. We all work very hard and in such a competitive world there really is no other way to win.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enduring frugality</strong>: We are frugal. We hate being wasteful and we are anti-luxury. A culture of cheapness keeps us young. We spend our cash wisely &amp; carefully — in a way that would make our grandmas proud.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bulldozing barriers</strong>: The world is malleable and we shape it. We truly believe this and act accordingly. We are relentlessly resourceful and are at the mercy of no-one but ourselves. You'll be shocked how capable you are and how much you can achieve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Keep your head down</strong>: We're boring people doing exciting work. We don't chase short-term status — we ignore short-term dopamine hits and focus on what matters. Outsiders will underestimate us and we revel in that.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The power of focus</strong>: We live in a world of power laws and we cannot overestimate the unimportance of practically everything. Know your One Thing, and nail it.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />🎯<em>"You just build a f</em>*ing amazing experience. Make each step amazing. Make every decision in the long term interest of the customer. Give the customer massively more value than you take."</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Compensation &amp; Benefits</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our compensation package includes equity, giving you the opportunity to share in what we build.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Training role</strong>: £13 per hour while you complete the required training and sign-off.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Qualified role</strong>: £15 per hour in total compensation, including equity, once you have completed the required training and are qualified and signed off for the role.</p></li></ul><h3>Benefits</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">The stuff below is cool as well.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Personal development</strong>: A £400 budget for books, courses and coaching to keep building your skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Personal wellness</strong>: A £400 budget for the gym and health apps to support your wellbeing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>GLP-1s</strong>: Get free membership with a clinic offering GLP-1s, if clinically applicable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Health coaching</strong>: Access free biweekly health coaching to help you stay healthy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work coaching</strong>: Access free biweekly work coaching to stay sharp and calm.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What are we missing?</strong> We're still early, so your ideas can help shape our culture.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/aios-yc-w20s21/warehouse-operative-blackburn-360966","tags":["Company"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Blackburn, Lancashire","created_at":1794120011},{"slug":"data-scientist-abingdon-335343","company_name":"Infinitesima","title":"Data Scientist","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Scientist | Semiconductor Metrology&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Abingdon, UK&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reward and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;£42,000 - £55,000 (depending on experience)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual bonus, 3x salary death in service benefit and private health care BUPA, EMI Share scheme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are a Data Scientist who enjoys turning instrument data into proof of what is possible, why not join us in Abingdon, Oxfordshire, and help prove the analysis methods behind advanced semiconductor metrology systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an ambitious and adaptable Data Scientist to join our new Data Science team in the Technology department, reporting to the Data Science Lead and working closely with our Modelling Scientist. You will generate and curate data, develop and test new algorithms, and benchmark them against what the instrument can physically deliver. When a method proves itself, you will package it for the Data Analysis team in Engineering, who turn it into robust product software. You will work with real customer use cases and wafer data from Applications Development, and proof-of-concept data from R&amp;amp;D.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an AI-first team, so you will use AI tools every day, while checking carefully what they produce. If your passion is speed, evidence and finding out what the data can really tell you, we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate synthetic data, and build and maintain the demo and performance data libraries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse instrument data to quantify noise and limitations, and help establish the information limit, meaning what is physically extractable from the instrument&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and test new algorithms and analysis methods (for example PCA, percentile methods and machine learning) on real and synthetic data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Benchmark methods against the information limit: achievable performance, measurement uncertainty, gauge R&amp;amp;R and drift contributors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clean, reproducible prototype code with test data and expected performance, ready to hand over to Data Analysis, and build analysis tools used across the Technology department&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tools every day to code, explore, analyse and report faster, verify what they produce, and present your results to the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education and experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree or above in Physics, Data Science, Applied Mathematics, Engineering or a similar subject, or [2] years’ relevant experience in data science or quantitative research&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and experience we’re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data analysis in Python (NumPy, SciPy, pandas, scikit-learn or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Heavy, day-to-day use of AI tools in your technical work, such as coding assistants and LLMs, with the judgement to verify their outputs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Image or signal processing, ideally on data from scientific instruments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Statistics applied to measurement data: uncertainty, repeatability, noise and drift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Machine learning methods, and how to validate them properly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, reproducible code and reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explaining results to technical and non-technical colleagues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious and adaptable, happy to work quickly and test ideas against the evidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’d love to see:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Atomic Force Microscopy or other nano-characterisation (SEM, FIB, profilometry), or semiconductor metrology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physics-based modelling or simulation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Version control (Git) and C#, and experience building agentic or AI-assisted analysis workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A bit about us:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Infinitesima is a privately owned company founded in 2001, as a spin-out of the University of Bristol, by CTO Professor Andrew Humphris. Our dynamic team of scientists and engineers is focussed on enabling the next generation of semiconductor devices through delivery of innovative products to customers around the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our strength lies in the varied perspectives that come from different cultures, experiences, and identities. We believe that true innovation is fuelled by collaboration, locally and globally. We strive to foster an environment where everyone can contribute meaningfully and thrive.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;If you require adjustments to take part in the recruitment process, please let us know, we’ll do our best to support you.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:210,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:210,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:300}&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your recruitment journey:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:210,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:210,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:300}&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We will interview you: Monday to Friday UK Time 9am to 4.30pm and we&#39;ll be as flexible as we can with Global Scheduling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:210,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:210,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:300}&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1st stage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;(45 minute) Remote meeting to evaluate your experience and technical ability&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
