<div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h3><strong>About the role</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Lead Data Scientist, you'll take on a pivotal, entrepreneurial role, functioning as the technical expert who thrives on complexity and commercial impact. You will be responsible for setting the technical direction and ensuring the high-quality, scalable delivery of our most challenging, high-impact projects.<br /><br />This position combines deep expertise in machine learning with strategic oversight to define project roadmaps, manage technical risk, and architect reliable solutions. Your focus will be on driving innovation, mentoring cross-functional teams, and actively shaping both our technical standards and long-term customer relationships.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h3><strong>What you'll be doing:</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Setting the technical direction for complex, business-critical projects and expertly balancing trade-offs between speed, innovation, and reliability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Designing and implementing reliable, production-grade technical solutions, ensuring comprehensive documentation of architectures and specifications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Defining project problems, developing clear roadmaps, and overseeing end-to-end delivery across multi-disciplinary workstreams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leading technical scoping and feasibility studies for high-value sales opportunities and strategic customer engagements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Managing relationships and communications with technical stakeholders, fostering trust and aligning technical solutions with shared long-term commercial goals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Driving the adoption of best practices, shared resources, and robust technical processes across the wider Data Science craft.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mentoring and developing other data scientists and team members, actively contributing to the growth and technical excellence of the organisation.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h3><strong>Who we're looking for:</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have proven project management expertise, capable of dividing complex, ill-defined problems into actionable, clearly defined workstreams with timelines you can defend.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You possess strong customer leadership skills, able to act as a trusted technical advisor and drive long-term strategic relationships with demanding clients.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You bring depth of expertise in at least one machine learning domain and strong technical breadth across the entire data science landscape.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a skilled technical leader, proficient in mentoring individuals, managing teams (including other managers), and rolling out impactful tools and workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are adept at managing ill-defined, high-risk tasks, consistently delivering innovative and practical outcomes under commercial pressure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You excel at cross-functional collaboration, effectively aligning technical strategy with Engineering, Commercial, and Infrastructure teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have experience extending technical oversight to business unit-level initiatives, using your vision to influence and contribute to organisational success.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h3><strong>The Interview Process</strong></h3><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Talent Team Screen (30 minutes)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Introduction to the team (30 minutes)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take Home Technical Assessment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical Interview (90 minutes)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercial Interview (60 minutes)</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Our Recruitment Ethos</strong></h2><h2></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We aim to grow the best team - not the most similar one. We know that diversity of individuals fosters diversity of thought, and that strengthens our principle of seeking truth. And we know from experience that diverse teams deliver better work, relevant to the world in which we live. We’re united by a deep intellectual curiosity and desire to use our abilities for measurable positive impact. We strongly encourage applications from people of all backgrounds, ethnicities, genders, religions and sexual orientations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you don’t feel you meet all the requirements, but are excited by the role and know you bring some key strengths, please don't hesitate in applying as you might be right for this role, or other roles. We are open to conversations about part-time hours. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">A note on AI: we're happy for you to use it for research and interview prep, but please don't use it to generate answers during live interviews. We also use an AI note-taker (Metaview) in interviews so interviewers can stay present (which you can opt out of just let us know,) and every application is reviewed by a human, never decided by AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/faculty/lead-data-scientist-london-220597","tags":["Data Science"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794109213},{"slug":"product-regulatory-counsel-london-466399","company_name":"Taptapsend","title":"Product & Regulatory Counsel","description":"<h2><strong>Tired of meeting the product at the terms and conditions stage?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Most product lawyers see the flow once it's built and the launch date is set. Here, you're on the whiteboard at ideation, so compliant by design is the plan, not the clean-up.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And the stakes are real. Taptap Send moves billions of dollars every month across 100 countries, and is now building wallets, cards and broader financial products for diaspora communities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The job</strong><br /></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll advise on new licensing and products from first idea to go-live, and own regulator engagement across our markets.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shape products before they're built:</strong> review designs, UX, flows and terms against regulatory and customer-outcome rules, Consumer Duty included, while change is still cheap.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turn regulation into decisions:</strong> what's mandatory, what's prudent, and the alternative route that still gets it launched.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the regulator relationship:</strong> across our markets, including new ones, and flag what regulatory change means for the roadmap early.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Take products to new countries:</strong> localise what already works, with country leads and local counsel.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build the playbooks:</strong> templates that let Legal scale without adding friction.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why you'll want it</strong><br /></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Spend your time on the hard questions.</strong> You're asked to shape our roadmap and launches, and understand how to fit them to the relevant regimes</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be a peer, with room to run.</strong> You'll join a flat team of regulatory and commercial lawyers, with real autonomy and a manager who trusts you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make launches faster, not slower.</strong> Legal in the room from day one is how products here ship sooner. That's the whole point of your seat.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make sending money home cheaper.</strong> Remittances pay for school fees, rent and medical bills, and are worth more than all foreign aid combined. Cheaper, reliable transfers put more of that money in families' hands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Is this you?</strong><br /></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're a qualified lawyer (UK or equivalent) with 4+ years' PQE in payments, e-money or financial services regulation, at a firm, a regulator or a fintech.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've advised payments or e-money firms under the FCA or an equivalent regime, dealt with the regulator directly, and helped product teams take live launches over the line.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You give the answer first and the reasoning second. Ambiguity across several jurisdictions doesn't stop you making the call.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>If you'd rather be asked first than asked last, apply. Missing a box or two? Send your CV anyway.</strong></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/taptapsend/product-regulatory-counsel-london-466399","tags":["Legal"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794109213},{"slug":"treasury-operations-analyst-london-84148","company_name":"Taptapsend","title":"Treasury Operations Analyst","description":"<h2><strong>Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Taptap Send is seeking a highly organised and motivated individual to join our Treasury Operations team and help us grow our business. In this role, you will report to the Director of Payments and touch all aspects of Taptap Send's payment operations, with an initial focus on stablecoin funding, working directly with our teams and partners across the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll own the full life cycle of payments, including creating, tracking and confirming crediting of funds, as well as troubleshooting payment issues across our growing Stablecoin operations. You'll also be involved in funding forecasts to ensure that our partners are well funded at all times.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work directly with our trading team as well as collaborating with the wider team that spans the globe ( London, Abidjan, Lagos, Nairobi, Paris and New York, to name a few places), ensuring that Taptap Send is effectively supported in its growth and customer ambitions! There is plenty of room for professional progression and personal growth within our friendly and ever-growing Taptap community.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2></h2><h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactively managing treasury operations, initially for stablecoins, to ensure our accounts are funded and payments can be processed seamlessly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working closely with partners to ensure that funding timelines are being delivered on time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Troubleshooting to find root causes of payment issues and working with internal and external partners to resolve</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assisting with onboarding new banks and trading partners for stablecoin, working closely with our business development team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Providing out-of-hours coverage when required</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Requirements</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have at least 1 years’ experience, ideally in a payments or funding role and/or working with stablecoins</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are passionate about our mission and eager to do what needs to be done to achieve it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are enthusiastic about treasury operations, solving unique problems, and optimizing processes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enjoy challenges, are resourceful and think outside the box to find creative ways to tackle problems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Love working in teams and building meaningful relationships with key stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Don’t hesitate to place a call to promptly resolve issues or persevere to get a result</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have great organisational skills and the ability to manage multiple time-sensitive priorities in a fast-paced startup environment where no two days are the same</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have proven analytical skills (Excel); SQL a plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are proficient in English</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Us</strong></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re building the world’s leading cross-border fintech for emerging markets - empowering families, fuelling local economies, and changing how millions access financial services.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since our launch in 2019, we have transformed how money moves across borders with our operations spanning 6 out of 7 continents and covering both the busiest and most underserved  (remittance) corridors. We tapped into a massive shift - from banks to phones - bringing digital finance to places where traditional systems never reached. The next stage of growth will fuel a network of services and products especially designed to make money more accessible to diaspora communities including local cards, and additional savings and payments features.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re growing fast, backed by world-class investors, and scaling a product that blends <strong>real world impact with cutting edge fintech innovation</strong>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here’s a little more:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Founded by Harvard grads and 3-time founders</strong> who previously built Segovia (acquired) and GiveDirectly (&gt;$300M revenue, fastest-growing NGO in the world)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Backed by top investors</strong> including Spark Capital, Canaan, Reid Hoffman, Breyer Capital, Unbound, Wamda, and more</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Built by global top performers</strong> from Bain, Google, McKinsey, Uber, Checkout, Bolt, and beyond - we move fast, stay humble, and care deeply about our mission</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Truly global team</strong> - 250+ people, 50+ nationalities, 50+ languages</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Guided by our values</strong> - ownership, impact, humility, and heart - in deed, not just word</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="postings-link" href="https://www.taptapsend.com/our-values"><u>Taptap Values </u></a></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Impact first</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team next</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Accept reality</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Propose solutions</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Win with grit</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be proactively candid, with yourself and others</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Love the particular</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own it</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create positive energy</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maybe, even have fun</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Taptap Send is an equal opportunity employer dedicated to building an inclusive and diverse workforce. All employment decisions are decided on the basis of qualifications, experience and business need. We strongly encourage applications who are members of underrepresented communities to apply.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you require reasonable adjustments to be made during the recruitment process, please do not hesitate to let us know. Any information you provide us in this respect will only be used to accommodate your requirements.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Note: we recognize imposter syndrome is real - any candidate that does not perfectly fit every characteristic of this role is still strongly encouraged to apply.  </em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/taptapsend/treasury-operations-analyst-london-84148","tags":["Treasury"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794109213},{"slug":"analytics-engineer-london-142133","company_name":"Taptapsend","title":"Analytics Engineer","description":"<h1><strong>Tired of being told “that’s not your scope”?</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plenty of good analysts hit the same wall: you query the data but never build the pipelines, you’re boxed into one lane, and more scope means waiting your turn. Here, it’s the opposite.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Taptap Send moves <strong>billions of dollars a month</strong> across <strong>6 of 7 continents</strong>. We’re probably the largest, fastest-growing money movement business you’ve never heard of. Cards, wallets, business-to-business payments, institutional payments, and new markets are all launching now, and each needs its data, reconciliations and reporting built from scratch. That’s your work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The job</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll own the external reports the business can’t operate without, then automate them into reliable, reusable dbt models. From day one you’ll work with Finance, Compliance, Treasury, Product and Data Engineering to make sure every number is modelled correctly.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own external reporting:</strong> deliver the datasets behind month-end close and regulatory reporting, on time, every cycle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Automate:</strong> turn multi-day manual work into scheduled pipelines, runbooks and dbt models, so it only gets done once.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Get ahead of launches:</strong> build reports and reconciliations as each product and market goes live, before anyone asks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be first line for data requests:</strong> build models so people and AI agents can answer repeat questions themselves.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Keep data trustworthy:</strong> build tests, checks and alerts that catch reconciliation breaks and stale data before they become incidents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Share what you know:</strong> peer-review code and join our weekly meetups.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Why you’ll want it</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow as fast as you’re able.</strong> We hire for potential, not years of experience. On a lean, talent-dense team, you’ll own real work early and take on more the moment you’re ready.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Go from querying data to designing systems. </strong>Data, product or business analyst? You don’t need to be an analytics engineer yet. Build the pipelines behind the numbers, and learn dbt, testing, automation and AI tooling from senior analytics engineers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Don't get boxed in. </strong>Own the reporting, automate it, then take on our biggest problems wherever they sit. Your hiring manager started in Finance and has since worked across Partner Ops, Fraud, Compliance, Reconciliation and Product.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>See the whole business.</strong> You’ll follow a transfer from the moment a customer taps send, through partner payout and reconciliation, to the report a regulator reads.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own numbers that matter.</strong> Auditors and Finance rely on what you build. This isn’t a dashboard role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Put more money in families’ hands.</strong> Remittances are a lifeline for millions of families and are worth more than all foreign aid. Every report you automate helps us keep transfers cheap and reliable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>You’ll fit if you have</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">1-2+ years in a data or analytics role</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">A technical or quantitative degree, or equivalent experience</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong SQL and experience wrangling messy, complex data</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Some experience automating repetitive work (e.g. scripts, scheduled jobs)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong sense of ownership: when something is broken, ownerless or late, you step in, fix it, and make sure it doesn’t happen again</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reliability under deadlines, a “no task too small” attitude, and comfort chasing stakeholders</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The right to work in the UK</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have:</strong> startup or scale-up experience, Python or R, dbt, Looker or Mode, and something you’ve built, at work or on the side, because the manual way annoyed you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sound like you? Apply, even if you don’t tick every box. We’d love to meet you.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/taptapsend/analytics-engineer-london-142133","tags":["Finance"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794109213},{"slug":"regional-marketing-intern-paris-207899","company_name":"Deliverect","title":"Regional Marketing Intern","description":"<div><span style="font-size: 11pt">At Deliverect, our API-first platform is revolutionizing commerce by providing a connected suite of on and off-premise solutions. We empower both the food and retail industries to expand their revenue and simplify their operations, creating seamless experiences for businesses to sell anywhere and deliver everywhere. Join us in this exciting journey, where your contributions will directly impact how businesses connect with their customers in a rapidly evolving global market.</span></div><div><br></div><div><strong><a href="https://www.deliverect.com/en" style="font-size: 18px;" class="postings-link">Deliverect</a></strong></div>
<div>
<p>En tant que licorne mondiale du SaaS en pleine expansion, Deliverect est à l’avant-garde de la révolution des solutions technologiques destinées aux secteurs dynamiques de l’hôtellerie-restauration et du « Q-commerce ».<br>Notre mission est claire : donner aux personnes ambitieuses les compétences et les connaissances nécessaires pour avoir un impact positif sur l’entreprise. Elles peuvent ainsi évoluer dans leur carrière tout en s’inscrivant dans un projet qui les dépasse.</p>
</div>
<h3><strong><span style="font-size: 18px;">Department Focus</span></strong></h3>
<div>
<p>Entrez dans l'univers du service marketing de Deliverect : une équipe dynamique composée de professionnels créatifs, axés sur les données et orientés vers les résultats, qui se consacrent corps et âme à la mission de Deliverect : donner aux entreprises les moyens d'offrir une expérience de commande exceptionnelle.<br>Nous ne nous contentons pas de placer les clients au cœur de nos stratégies ; nous les mettons véritablement à l'honneur, en comprenant leurs besoins et leurs aspirations afin de concevoir des campagnes marketing qui trouvent véritablement un écho auprès d'eux.</p>
</div>
<div>
<p>Les données sont au cœur de notre activité : elles constituent le moteur qui guide chacune de nos décisions, de la stratégie de campagne à la mise en œuvre créative. L'efficacité de nos campagnes ne se limite pas à une simple évaluation ; il s'agit d'un processus continu qui nous permet d'adopter des tactiques agiles et de nous adapter en permanence à un environnement en constante évolution.<br>La collaboration est notre mot d'ordre : nous travaillons en étroite collaboration avec les autres services de Deliverect pour développer et mettre en œuvre des initiatives en parfaite adéquation avec nos objectifs commerciaux globaux.</p>
