re Development</strong> – Design, prototype, and maintain mechanical test fixtures, jigs, and tooling built for reliability, reproducibility, and repeatable operator use.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mechanical Integration</strong> – Design the physical integration of sensors, actuators, cameras, and other instruments into test stations, in collaboration with the Automation Software Engineers who own the control and software layer. Occasional software integration is also possible based on candidate skillset.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ATE Integration </strong>— Specify and integrate custom solutions from external vendors for testing equipment/instrumentation (RF housings, GNSS, optical systems…).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-Team Collaboration</strong> – Work closely with product development, manufacturing, and the <em>Infrastructure &amp; Deployment</em> engineer to deliver robust, maintainable, and scalable automation solutions for the factory and field.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h3><strong>Candidate Requirements</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">MSc in Mechanical, Mechatronics, or related engineering field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent CAD skills with experience in rapid prototyping and robust solution implementation (SolidWorks, Catia or similar).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with external vendors and machine shops for part fabrication and test equipment selection.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable performing soldering, wiring, and small-scale electrical circuit work for test system integration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with electronic assemblies (PCBAs); familiarity with pogo-pin / bed-of-nails fixtu