&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/flexport/account-executive-enterprise-448992","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1794045316},{"slug":"project-manager-innovation-bank-transaction-systems-zurich-287179","company_name":"coni+partner AG","title":"Project Manager Innovation Bank Transaction Systems","description":"<p>coni + partner, established 1993, is a consultancy company with headquarters in Zurich and subsidiaries in Düsseldorf and Shanghai. We are specialised in custom-fit staffing in tune with the corporate culture by ensuring a perfect match of professional skills, references and personal as well as social skills of successful candidates.</p><p>Our client is an international bank in Zurich. We are searching for a payment or transaction specialist (m, f, d) as</p><p><strong>Project Manager Innovation Bank Transaction Systems </strong></p><p>Your Tasks: </p><p>As a member of a team responsible for the smooth functioning of payment system operations / Analyse all incoming/outgoing payments e.g. large-value and mass payments in connection with services provided by financial market participants / Analyse the interbank alerts and the bank's crisis organization / Promoting the continuous improvement of payment processes and transformative change across the bank, including AI and its potential applications within the filtering systems designed to combat sanctions and payment fraud / Working closely with the business and IT teams to support colleagues with complex issues, with the aim of improving efficiency, the quality of transactions and services as well as operational stability / Monitoring transaction regulations and ensuring compliance with new regulatory standards by providing support with their implementation / Ensure that the process and control documentation is updated / Point of contact for enquiries regarding payment transactions and customer support / Involvement in various projects.</p><p>Your Profile:</p><p>Master’s or Bachelor’s with focus on Banking & Finance or Business Informatics / Professional experience with national and international payments as well as knowledge of the entire payments lifecycle / Sound knowledge of payment systems and  operational controls of a bank / Experience as a project manager in the banking sector, in management consultancy (e.g. with the ‘Big 4’) or in strategy consultancy, combined with the specialist expertise to drive the adoption of AI within the bank / Know-how as project or sub-project leader providing business expertise to local and international projects / Ability to approach projects methodically and in a structured manner, and problem-solving skills / Ability to link different subject areas, as well as ‘holistic thinking’ / Self-starter and networker / Strong communication and negotiation skills / Strong interpersonal skills / German and English.</p><p>Your Contact:</p><p>Mr. Ivano Coni would like to support you. Your application will be kept strictly confidential.</p><p></p><p><strong>coni + partner ag</strong></p><p>Ivano Coni</p><p>Managing Director</p><p>Klosbachstrasse 107</p><p>CH-8032 -----<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/conipartner-ag/project-manager-innovation-bank-transaction-systems-zurich-287179","tags":["Project Management"],"job_types":["Indefinite contract (unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag)","manager"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1794034852},{"slug":"system-architect-zurich-244383","company_name":"Hyperscale Power","title":"System Architect","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Hyperscale Power is building the power backbone for the AI data center era: a complete power conversion chain from 13.8kV–35kV medium-voltage AC down to 800V DC, combining ultra-compact SiC-based power blocks. Our Solid-State Transformers (SSTs) are the core of this revolution, providing unprecedented control, efficiency, and compactness.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a System Architect, you will be responsible for our solid-state transformer as a complete system. You will connect the work of our power electronics, magnetics, and mechanical and thermal engineering teams into one coherent system, and ensure it meets the requirements of hyperscale data center customers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Instead of specializing in a single subsystem, your mission is to keep the whole system in view: balancing efficiency, size, cost, reliability and manufacturability, guiding the key technical trade-offs, and taking our SST from prototype to a product ready for certification and series production.<br /><br /><strong>This role is for you if…</strong><br />you’ve owned a complex high-power system rather than one part of it. You enjoy keeping the whole picture in view, making the call on trade-offs between expert teams, and bringing just enough structure to a fast-moving team without slowing it down.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>This role isn’t for you if…</strong><br />you’ve spent your career going deep on a single component or subsystem, or you manage projects without making the technical decisions yourself. It’s also not a fit if you need a fixed specification and established processes before you can start.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the system architecture of the SST and its key performance metrics, including efficiency, power density, cost, thermal performance, reliability, manufacturability and control performance.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate the subsystems of the SST (AC/DC, DC/DC, magnetics, mechanical and thermal) and their interfaces, ensuring the work of each team is compatible and consistent with the system design.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead system-level trade-off decisions and set technical priorities across teams.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and maintain system requirements, interface specifications and change management, ensuring design changes are assessed for their impact across the system.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate the requirements of data center operators and hyperscalers into system specifications, and track how they evolve.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Explore and compare different system architectures and their integration in the datacenter power supply chain</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive standardization and design for manufacturing across subsystems in preparation for series production.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with the compliance and certification team to define a feasible certification path for the system.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify technical risks at system level early and propose mitigations.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Qualifications</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">MSc or a higher degree in Electrical Engineering or a related discipline.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">8+ years of industry experience in developing complex power electronic systems.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven responsibility at system or platform level, e.g. as system engineer, system architect, technical lead or team lead.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record of taking power electronic systems from development to series product.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with high-power systems such as EV charging, electric drivetrains, rail traction, industrial drives, renewable energy converters or robotics.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Broad understanding of the electrical, magnetic, thermal, mechanical and control aspects of power electronic systems, and how they interact.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of cooling concepts and the mechanical integration of high-power electronics.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with standards, norms and certification processes for power electronic products.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication and decision-making skills; able to align experts across disciplines and drive decisions.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working in a fast-paced startup environment with evolving requirements.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">The job will be located at our HQ in Egg b. Zürich, Switzerland.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with medium-voltage converter systems or solid-state transformers.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of data center power architectures.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in design for manufacturing and cost engineering.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience establishing systems engineering processes in a growing organization.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equity + competitive salary.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unique technology and market opportunity – shape the architecture of a new product category for the energy transition.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid work with flexible working times.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/hyperscale-power/system-architect-zurich-244383","tags":["Research & Development"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1794033630},{"slug":"business-risk-analyst-trading-desks-bank-zurich-148970","company_name":"coni+partner AG","title":"Business Risk Analyst Trading Desks Bank","description":"<p></p><p>coni + partner, established 1993, is a consultancy company with headquarters in Zurich and subsidiaries in Düsseldorf and Shanghai. We are specialised in custom-fit staffing in tune with the corporate culture by ensuring a perfect match of professional skills, references and personal as well as social skills of successful candidates.</p><p>Our client is an international bank in Zurich. We are looking for a trading process specialist (m, f, d) as </p><p><strong>Business Risk Analyst Trading Desks Bank</strong></p><p>Your Tasks: </p><p>Conducting analyses of the Bank’s trading processes, operational risks and compliance (e.g. EMIR, MiFID II)  / Identifying control gaps and developing solutions or optimising trading processes based on control deficiencies identified following audits in this area / Supporting the trading department in developing process and IT adjustments / Further developing and maintaining a robust control framework within the trading department / Establishing controls for the second line of defence to optimise compliance with trading regulations / Working closely with IT, the Trading and Legal & Compliance departments, as well as external specialists, to implement trading-related policies to ensure clearly defined roles and responsibilities / Planning and conducting audits to ensure compliance and minimise risks associated with applicable laws and regulations / Preparing assessments of trading-related risks / Ad hoc project work in response to specific incidents to systematically eliminate vulnerabilities in trading systems / Point of contact for the business division on compliance matters.</p><p>Your Profile:</p><p>Master’s or Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration or Business Informatics / Experience with trading processes as a Business Risk Analyst at a bank or as a bank auditor / Knowledge of investment banking, financial markets and financial products, and the regulatory environment / Understanding of financial market infrastructure activities / Familiarity with process risks in trading and knowledge of the relevant regulations / Strong analytical and conceptual skills, as well as a structured and solution-oriented approach to work / Team-oriented with a high degree of personal responsibility and assertiveness / Ability to communicate clearly, negotiate skillfully and get everyone on board / Ability to meet deadlines precisely and set priorities / IT proficiency / Proficiency in MS Office (Excel) / German and English, both languages spoken fluently.</p><p>Your Contact:</p><p>Mr. Ivano Coni will be happy to help you. Your application will be kept strictly confidential.</p><p></p><p><strong>coni + partner ag</strong></p><p>Ivano Coni</p><p>Managing Director</p><p>Klosbachstrasse 107</p><p>CH-8032 -----<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/conipartner-ag/business-risk-analyst-trading-desks-bank-zurich-148970","tags":["Business Analyst"],"job_types":["Indefinite contract (unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag)","professional / experienced"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1794033050},{"slug":"senior-risk-analyst-lombard-kredite-zurich-191006","company_name":"coni+partner AG","title":"Senior Risk Analyst Lombard Kredite","description":"<p>coni + partner ist ein seit 1993 bestehendes Beratungshaus mit Sitz in Zürich und Niederlassungen in Düsseldorf und Shanghai. Unsere Stärke ist die passgenaue Besetzung von Positionen entsprechend der Unternehmenskultur, unter genauer Betrachtung fachlicher Kompetenzen, Referenzen und «soft skills» der Kandidaten.</p><p>Unser Kunde ist eine Privat Bank in Zürich.  Wir suchen einen Kreditspezialisten (m, w, d) als </p><p><strong>Senior Risk Analyst Lombard Kredite</strong></p><p>Ihre Aufgaben:</p><p>Risikomanagement komplexer Lombard-Finanzierungen für Private Banking Kunden (HNWI/UHNWI) / Analyse und Überwachung von Finanzierungstransaktionen in einem marktnahen und dynamischen Umfeld mit grosser Produktvielfalt / Analyse und Entscheid von Kreditanträgen aus dem Bereich des Structured Lombard unter kredittechnischen, finanzwirtschaftlichen, juristischen und reputationsbezogenen Gesichtspunkten /  Mitarbeit in fachspezifischen Projekten / Mitgestaltung von Prozessen und Methoden /  Weitreichende Kompetenzen und Verantwortlichkeiten.</p><p>Ihr Profil:</p><p>Master oder Bachelor in Betriebswirtschaft / Berufserfahrung und  Erfahrung im Lombard- bzw. Structured Finance-Risikomanagement / Kenntnis der gängigen Produkte (Equities, Fixed Income, Structured Credit sowie Derivate) und Handelsstrategien (long/short, Arbitrage etc.) / Kenntnisse im Kredit- bzw. Kreditportfoliomanagement auch aus methodischer Sicht / Sehr gute Deutsch- und Englischkenntnisse.</p><p>Ihr Kontakt:</p><p>Herr Ivano Coni ist gerne für Sie da. Ihre Bewerbung wird streng vertraulich behandelt.</p><p></p><p><strong>coni + partner ag</strong></p><p>Ivano Coni</p><p>Managing Director</p><p>Klosbachstrasse 107</p><p>CH-8032 -----<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/conipartner-ag/senior-risk-analyst-lombard-kredite-zurich-191006","tags":["Credit Analysis"],"job_types":["Unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag","berufserfahren"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1794033050},{"slug":"senior-multiphysics-rd-engineer-electro-mechanical-satigny-374681","company_name":"Secheron S Dot A","title":"Senior Multiphysics R&D Engineer (Electro-mechanical)","description":"<p>With over 140 years of Swiss engineering heritage, Sécheron Hasler Group is a global leader in high-power electrical and electronic equipment. Our solutions power railways, renewable energy, DC and AC networks, and industrial systems worldwide trusted for their precision, reliability, and innovation.</p><p>At the heart of modern rail infrastructure, our Traction Power Systems unit delivers cutting-edge DC and AC traction substations, protection systems, power conversion and digital monitoring solutions. Join us to shape the future of sustainable mobility with technology that keeps cities and countries moving. For the expansion of our team, we are seeking to hire in&nbsp;Geneva a dynamic and motivated Senior R&amp;D Engineer.</p><p> </p><p>As a Senior Multiphysics R&amp;D Engineer, you will be involved with the R&amp;D team in the development of cutting-edge high-speed switching devices such as high-speed DC circuit breakers, contributing to the full product lifecycle: from design to application.</p><p>You will work at the intersection of electrical and mechanical engineering, bringing expertise in power electronics, dielectrics and thermal advanced modeling, playing a key role in shaping the future of medium voltage switching technology.</p><p></p><p><strong>Main Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul><li>Contribute to innovative R&amp;D projects focused on high-speed circuit breakers and related switching technologies.</li><li>Design and simulate electrical switching systems using MATLAB/Simulink, COMSOL MultiPhysics including electromagnetic, thermal, material science and dielectric behavior.</li><li>Define and execute test plans for prototypes, including dielectric, thermal, and mechanical validation.</li><li>Interface with cross-functional teams including mechanical, electrical and electronics engineers.</li><li>Collaborate with manufacturing teams to optimize material processing and industrialization.</li><li>Mentor junior engineers and contribute to technical strategy and innovation roadmaps.</li><li>Contribute to patent filings, technical documentation, and compliance with IEC/IEEE standards.</li><li>Develop and validate electronic control boards for switching and protection systems.</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Minimum 8 years of experience in R&amp;D for low voltage and/or medium voltage electric equipment.</li><li>Good understanding of Railway protection systems – Modern DC microgrids.</li><li>English fluent mandatory, French strong plus.</li><li>Master’s or PhD in Electrical Engineering, Power Electronics, Applied Physics or similar.</li><li>Strong understanding of electro-mechanical and magnetic systems.</li></ul><p><strong>Strong plus:</strong></p><ul><li>Experience with testing and validation in high-voltage environments.</li><li>Knowledge of High-speed DC circuit breakers.</li></ul><p><strong>Plus:</strong></p><ul><li>Good knowledge in power electronics switching devices.</li><li>Thermal and dielectric analysis.</li><li>Modeling and simulation in MATLAB/Simulink - COMSOL.</li><li>Material processing and manufacturing techniques.</li><li>Electronic board design and integration.</li><li>CAD 3D design tools (SolidWorks).</li><li>Curious, attentive to detail, team player.</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><p>We foster&nbsp;flat hierarchies&nbsp;and&nbsp;direct communication, enabling quick decisions and strong collaboration across all levels. You’ll be trusted with real responsibility and encouraged to take initiative, with plenty of opportunities to grow both personally and professionally.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/secheron-s-dot-a/senior-multiphysics-rd-engineer-electro-mechanical-satigny-374681","tags":["Engineering","Electrical/Electronic Manufacturing","Sécheron | Electrical Safety Solutions"],"job_types":["Full time","mid-senior"],"location":"Satigny, Switzerland","created_at":1794032418},{"slug":"financial-mathematician-portfolio-risk-asset-management-zurich-26595","company_name":"coni+partner AG","title":"Financial Mathematician Portfolio Risk Asset Management","description":"<p>coni + partner, established 1993, is a consultancy company with headquarter in Zurich and subsidiaries in Düsseldorf and Shanghai. We are specialised in custom-fit staffing in tune with the corporate culture by ensuring a perfect match of professional skills, references and personal as well as social skills of successful candidates.</p><p>Our client is the asset management of an international bank in Zurich. We are looking for a quantitative finance specialist (m, f, d) as a</p><p><strong>Financial Mathematician Portfolio Risk Asset Management </strong></p><p>Your Tasks:</p><p>Risk- and performance-oriented quantitative analysis and calculations for a wide range of asset classes including fund investments in the field of the bank's asset management / Foster in-depth risk analyses, estimates and recommendations based on high quality assessments using e.g. Bloomberg, Morningstar, RiskMetrix, etc. /  Monitoring of risk positions in the investment portfolios / Preparation of reports containing risk analytics and key performance indicators for internal and external stakeholders / Refine methodologies to constantly expand the analysis and reporting capabilities / Optimizing asset management strategies, products, processes and tools / Work closely with other team members, portfolio managers and senior management / Regular reporting to the Head of Asset Management / Participation in projects focused on the continuous development of infrastructure, tools and methods.</p><p>Your Profile:</p><p>Master in Finance or Quantitative Finance / Professional experience in asset management at a bank or a major fund manager, or in fund auditing / Experience in risk & performance calculation across equity, fixed income, multi-asset and fund portfolios, including private equity Investments / Experience with a broad range of  portfolio calculations e.g. portfolio risk calculations, sensitivity analysis, factor exposures, concentration limits, liquidity risk, tracking error, etc. / Experience with investment restriction set up and controlling / Extensive experience with Bloomberg, Morningstar, RiskMetrix, etc. essential / Programming skills: SQL, VBA and Python, etc., for the further development of various in-house tools / Strong analytical skills / Team-oriented with process oriented thinking and problem solving mentality / Ability to go into details and to communicate the results to internal stakeholders and investors.</p><p>Your Contact:</p><p>Mr. Ivano Coni would like to support you. Your application will be kept strictly confidential.</p><p></p><p><strong>coni + partner ag</strong></p><p>Ivano Coni</p><p>Managing Director</p><p>Klosbachstrasse 107</p><p>8032 Zürich</p><p>Tel.: +41 44 254 90 10</p><p>E-Mail: ----- </p><p></p><p></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/conipartner-ag/financial-mathematician-portfolio-risk-asset-management-zurich-26595","tags":["Asset","Fonds Management"],"job_types":["Indefinite contract (unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag)","professional / experienced"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1794031273},{"slug":"delivery-transformation-principal-zurich-18081","company_name":"thoughtworks","title":"Delivery Transformation Principal","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;description content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced and dynamic &lt;strong&gt;Delivery Transformation Principal&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;to drive the successful execution and delivery of complex transformation projects and key work-streams. The ideal candidate is a hands-on practitioner and subject matter expert with a proven track record of delivering challenging, high-impact projects at top-tier consulting or digital engineering firms. This is a unique opportunity to lead the end-to-end delivery of critical client workstreams whilst actively shaping our modern agile practices and mentoring high-performing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;job-responsibilities&quot;&gt;Job responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-responsibilities content&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Delivery Leadership: &lt;/strong&gt;Lead the planning, execution, and delivery of complex, high-risk transformation projects and core workstreams. Solve ambiguous delivery challenges, unblock technical and operational dependencies, and champion agile ways of working to ensure initiatives are delivered on time, within budget, and to the highest quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Relationship Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and maintain strong, trusted relationships with senior client stakeholders and department leads. Act as a trusted delivery advisor, guide stakeholders through technical and delivery trade-offs, and navigate difficult or sensitive conversations with diplomacy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership and Program Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Provide hands-on mentorship and constructive feedback to cross-functional project teams, fostering a culture of continuous learning and accountability. Oversee day-to-day workstream execution, sprint planning, and team operational health, while supporting internal capability building and interviewing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth and Business Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify and pursue opportunities for project extension and process improvements within existing accounts. Partner with client leads and solution teams by evaluating statements of work, scoping delivery efforts, and contributing technical delivery insights to proposals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;job-qualifications&quot;&gt;Job qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-qualifications content&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;professional-skills&quot;&gt;Professional Skills&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;skills inner-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of total professional experience, including 4+ years leading complex project delivery or agile workstreams within a management consultancy, technology consulting firm, or digital engineering services company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success in leading and delivering complex, multi-disciplinary software or digital transformation programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience in &lt;strong&gt;managing fixed price and outcome based deliveries&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication, facilitation, and influencing skills with the ability to articulate complex concepts and handle objections across senior stakeholder groups.&lt;/li&gt;
