&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/redwoodsoftware/principle-software-engineer-87856","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1794002117},{"slug":"chief-financial-officer-amsterdam-88547","company_name":"Fastned","title":"Chief Financial Officer","description":"<p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Fastned is on a mission to accelerate the transition to electric mobility. Since 2012, we have been building and operating a rapidly growing network of iconic fast-charging stations across Europe powered entirely by solar and wind energy. With 500+ colleagues, we now operate over 450+ stations across nine countries, with an ambitious goal of reaching 1,000 stations by 2030. We are not building infrastructure for its own sake. Every station we open is a tangible step in the transition away from fossil fuels.</span></strong></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">We are a listed company on Euronext Amsterdam, with a community of over 10,000 retail investors and a growing base of institutional funding partners. In 2025, we reported €122.4 million in charging revenue: a 47% year-on-year increase, exceeding €100 million in annual revenue for the first time. Fastned is at a pivotal point: growing fast, approaching profitability, and expanding across Europe. As our CFO, you will lead a talented and growing team of 40+ finance professionals to drive and shape Fastned's continued success.</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">&nbsp;</span></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#121317">Your Role</span><span style="color:#5a5f72">&nbsp;</span></strong></h3><p><span style="color:#121317">We are looking for a CFO to join the Management Board, alongside our CEO, COO and CCO, who will drive Fastned on its path to profitability while enabling further growth.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">This role is for a financial leader who thrives in scale-up environments and feels comfortable navigating the complexity of an international matrix organisation. You know how to build a finance function that is both structured and able to move fast, effectively resolving scaling-bottlenecks along the way. You maintain strong financial discipline while enabling the continued investment needed to expand the charging network that supports our long-term vision.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">In this role, you oversee the full Finance domain, developing people and teams to the next phase. You act as a key financial voice within the Executive Team and Management Board.</span></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#121317">Your responsibilities will include:</span></strong></h3><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Strategic Planning &amp; Partnering</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">: Partner with the Executive Board to set long-term financial goals, evaluate investment opportunities, oversee mergers and acquisitions and direct your teams to deliver the analyses and frameworks that underpin these decisions.&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Manage our capital structure</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> by optimising the company's capital, debt, and equity structure to maximise shareholder value.</span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Leading the Finance Domain: </span></strong><span style="color:#000000">lead and inspire a talented Finance team of 43 professionals, bringing clear direction, fostering growth in culture that balances a bold mission with financial rigour. With your </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">operational finance expertise</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">, you will empower domain leads to do their best work. For each of your domains this entails the following:</span></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Accounting &amp; Reporting team: </span></strong><span style="color:#000000">enabling finance transformation to ensure accurate and timely preparation of financial statements, ensuring full compliance with applicable regulatory standards and accounting frameworks.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Funding &amp; Investor Relations team: </span></strong><span style="color:#000000">develop a compelling, forward-looking equity story that reflects both current performance and long-term potential. You will serve as the primary spokesperson for Fastned's financial health, leading earnings calls and maintaining strong relationships with analysts, shareholders, and investors.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Business &amp; Financial Control team: </span></strong><span style="color:#000000">partner with Country- and Functional Directors to evaluate the business cases for new markets, charging stations, joint ventures, and other expansion initiatives, balancing rigorous financial discipline and cost efficiency with growth decisions.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Risk &amp; Audit team: </span></strong><span style="color:#000000">build structures that protect against financial fraud and operational risk. Represent the Management Board in Audit Committee meetings and actively drive the implementation and maintenance of internal controls.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Tax team: </span></strong><span style="color:#000000">meet tax compliance and the maintenance of a tax control framework across all countries, covering corporate income tax, transfer pricing, and VAT.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Serve as the executive owner of Fastned's sustainability strategy, ensuring it is credible, auditable, and aligned with both regulatory requirements, the company's long-term mission.</span></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Management Board Member</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">: Serve as a full member of the Management Board, carrying </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">statutory responsibility</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> for Fastned's financial governance, risk management, sustainability reporting, and knowing when to accelerate growth and when to apply disciplined challenges.</span></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#000000">Who we are looking for</span></strong></h3><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">A financial leader</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> (RA, CPA, CIMA, ACA or equivalent) with proven experience in senior </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">operational finance</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> leadership in scale-up or high-growth environments.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">A genuine people leader</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> who inspires, challenges, and grows the people around them.&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Experience in </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">building and professionalising a scalable finance function</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">, including systems, processes, and team capability including leveraging AI and digital technologies company-wide.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Bring a healthy appetite for risk combined with rigorous financial discipline: knowing when to accelerate and when to challenge, </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">driving the business towards profitability while enabling sustainable growth.&nbsp;</span></strong></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Good understanding of funding</span><strong><span style="color:#000000"> </span></strong><span style="color:#000000">and capital markets including bonds, equity, project finance, or institutional investment with the</span><strong><span style="color:#000000"> ability to tell a compelling and credible financial story to investors.</span></strong></p></li>