</li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">An enthusiastic, professional, and international team</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Regular team events, including off-sites and fun activities</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Unlimited skin checks for you</span></p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/skinvision/senior-ux-designer-amsterdam-229420","tags":["Product Development"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1793946684},{"slug":"senior-growth-marketing-manager-rotterdam-462174","company_name":"AIHR","title":"Senior Growth Marketing Manager","description":"<p><span style="color:#000000">Are you an ambitious growth marketer with an entrepreneurial spirit and a track record of scaling customer acquisition? Do you love diving into data, spotting opportunities, and turning ideas into measurable growth? Are you excited by opening new acquisition channels and finding smarter ways to grow in an AI-driven world?</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">AIHR is looking for an experienced Senior Growth Marketing Manager</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> to help accelerate growth across our B2C and B2B businesses. You'll work across the entire acquisition funnel, from scaling paid media and improving conversion to launching new growth initiatives that drive MQLs and revenue.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">You'll join an ambitious, results-driven Growth Marketing team, working closely with our specialists to challenge existing approaches, experiment with new ideas, and deliver results. You'll have the autonomy to lead initiatives, the support of an experienced team, and the opportunity to make a direct impact on a global e-learning business.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">About AIHR</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Founded in 2016 with the mission to future-proof HR, the </span><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.aihr.com/"><span style="color:#1155CC">Academy to Innovate HR (AIHR)</span></a></u><span style="color:#000000"> has become the world’s market leader in online training for human resources (HR) professionals. We have a global customer base spread across 140+ countries, amongst which companies like Unilever, Reckitt, Goldman Sachs, Philips, Deloitte, Nike, Heineken, and UBS. It is our goal to continuously upskill and empower 1,000,000 HR Professionals.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">We are an international team of 100+ people, driven by excellence, innovation, and a hunger to grow in everything we do. As such, we strive to provide the world’s best courses and excellent support to our customers while continuously optimizing every aspect of our work. With over 30 nationalities, our team is diverse, yet we all share a few traits: we're friendly, enthusiastic, and great team players.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Being a fast-growing company, working at AIHR means taking on a lot of responsibility and getting countless opportunities to develop yourself in new areas and the potential to craft your own role.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Role and Responsibilities</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">As our Senior Growth Marketing Manager, you'll play a key role in accelerating customer acquisition across our B2C and B2B businesses. Working closely with the Head of Growth Marketing and VP of Marketing, you'll help us achieve our ambitious growth targets, improve acquisition efficiency, and identify new opportunities to scale.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">A core part of your role will be diving into performance data to understand what's working, what's not, and where our biggest growth opportunities lie. You'll work closely with our Performance Marketing Specialist to scale paid acquisition, challenge existing strategies, test new approaches, and support campaign execution where needed. You'll also collaborate with our CRO Specialist to identify opportunities across landing pages, website journeys, and conversion funnels, turning insights into experiments that drive more leads and revenue.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">You'll bring a strong growth perspective to our email marketing efforts, working with the team to analyze nurture flows, promotional campaigns, and audience segments, and identify opportunities to improve performance. Beyond optimizing existing channels, you'll explore, launch, and scale new acquisition opportunities, including those emerging from the changing AI- and LLM-driven marketing landscape.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Most importantly, this is a hands-on role where you'll do more than develop strategies and bring ideas to the table. You'll actively execute initiatives yourself or work closely with the wider team to bring them to life. Whether you're launching a new campaign, testing an acquisition channel, or improving conversion, you'll take ownership of turning opportunities into measurable business results.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">On a typical week</span></strong><br></p><p><span style="color:#000000">It's Monday morning, and you start the week with a coffee and a look at last week's acquisition performance. You open GA4, HubSpot, and your marketing dashboards to see how we're tracking against our B2C and B2B MQL targets. While digging into the data, you notice that one of our paid campaigns is generating plenty of traffic, but conversions have dropped. You investigate further, identify a few potential causes, and head into the Growth Marketing stand-up with some ideas to improve performance.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">After the stand-up, you catch up with our Performance Marketing Specialist to review campaign performance and discuss opportunities to scale. You identify a promising new audience and agree to test a different creative approach. Rather than just handing over your ideas, you jump into the advertising platform to help set up the campaign and work with the team to get the new creatives ready for launch.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">On Tuesday, you're focused on improving our B2B acquisition funnel. You've spotted an opportunity to increase conversions on the AI for HR Boot Camp landing page. You meet with our B2B Marketer and CRO Specialist to review the data, discuss your hypothesis, and agree on an experiment. You brief the team, align with sales on the proposed changes, and help move the experiment towards launch.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Wednesday is a work-from-home day, giving you time to dive deeper into our acquisition strategy. You've been exploring how AI and LLMs are changing the way HR professionals discover training providers. You identify a potential new acquisition opportunity, research the market, and put together a practical plan to test it. Later, you meet with the Head of Growth Marketing to challenge your assumptions, refine the approach, and agree on the next steps.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">On Thursday, you review the performance of our B2C email nurture flows with the Email Marketing team. You notice an opportunity to improve conversions from leads to MQLs and propose a change to the messaging and sequence. After lunch with colleagues in the office, you turn your attention to an upcoming quarterly campaign, working with the wider Marketing team to finalize the messaging and coordinate the launch. You also start investigating new channels that could help expand the campaign's reach and attract new audiences.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Friday starts with reviewing the results of a recent landing page experiment. The changes have improved conversion, so you work with the CRO Specialist to roll them out more broadly. You also catch up with our BizOps team to improve HubSpot reporting, ensuring we have better visibility into acquisition performance and opportunities for growth. Before wrapping up the week, you review progress against our growth priorities, share your findings with the team, and identify the next opportunities worth pursuing.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">After a productive week of analyzing, experimenting, and driving initiatives forward, you close your laptop and join your colleagues for Friday drinks.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">We offer</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A revenue-generating role in a fast-growing scale-up company;&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Competitive, benchmarked compensation;</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A high degree of autonomy in a vibrant, result-driven, inclusive, and international team;</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><span style="color:#0E101A">A beautiful office right across Rotterdam Central Station (Milleniumtower) and a satellite office in Amsterdam;</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><span style="color:#0E101A">26 paid holidays per year + 1 extra day for the first 5 years you work at AIHR</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#0E101A">Exchange any 2 public holiday days for 2 other days of your choice;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#0E101A">Work from anywhere policy, where you can work abroad for 20 days in a calendar year;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#0E101A">Pension plan;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#0E101A">4 Trust days per year (ad-hoc recovery days to take whenever you're overwhelmed, exhausted, or need to deal with something personal);</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#0E101A">Access to OpenUp mental health platform;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Personal development budget, training, and we pay for the books you read;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">All public transport expenses covered (NS Business Card);</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">MacBook + all other equipment you need to do your work;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Daily lunch prepared by a chef, weekly drinks, and fun team activities;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Free access to the office gym.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#000000">Get a taste of AIHR experience and check out our </span><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://aihr.recruitee.com/benefits-guide"><span style="color:#1155CC">AIHR Benefits Guide</span></a></u><span style="color:#000000">!</span></p> <br> <p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Who you are</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">We're looking for an ambitious, data-driven, and commercially minded growth marketer with an entrepreneurial spirit. Someone who loves identifying opportunities, challenging existing approaches, and turning ideas into measurable results. You're not just a strategic thinker; you're equally excited about getting operational, executing ideas yourself, and making things happen.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">You have:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">8+ years of experience in growth marketing, with a proven track record of scaling customer acquisition, ideally across both B2C and B2B businesses in SaaS, e-learning, or other high-growth industries;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Demonstrable experience scaling paid acquisition campaigns, including managing or scaling advertising budgets of €100,000+ per month;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to dive into performance data, identify growth opportunities, and translate insights into actionable initiatives;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A strong understanding of full-funnel marketing, including paid acquisition, CRO, landing page optimization, email marketing, and growth economics such as CAC and LTV;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Strong experience with HubSpot or comparable CRM platforms, including segmentation, automation, lifecycle marketing, attribution, and reporting;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Experience identifying, testing, and scaling new acquisition channels and growth opportunities;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Strong AI proficiency, with experience using ChatGPT and Claude to analyze data, improve workflows, and accelerate execution;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">An understanding of how AI and LLMs are changing customer acquisition, with a forward-thinking approach to emerging marketing channels;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A proactive, hands-on approach, with the ability to independently lead and execute initiatives while collaborating effectively with the wider team;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, with a collaborative mindset, openness to feedback, and a hunger to grow;</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Bonus:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Experience in event marketing, community-led growth, or account-based marketing (ABM).</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Apply for the job</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Are you excited to become our new Senior Growth Marketing Manager? Then we'd love to hear from you! We are looking to hire for this role as soon as we find an eligible candidate.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">P.S. </span></strong><span style="color:#000000">Research shows that while men apply to jobs when they meet an average of 60% of the criteria, women tend to apply only when they meet 100% of them. So if you think you have what it takes, but don't necessarily meet every single point above, please still apply. We'd love to consider you and see if you could be a great fit.&nbsp;</span></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/aihr/senior-growth-marketing-manager-rotterdam-462174","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Rotterdam, Zuid-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1793946684},{"slug":"senior-php-backend-developer-zoetermeer-85077","company_name":"SHIFTBASE B.V.","title":"Senior PHP Backend Developer","description":"<h3 style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">About Shiftbase</span></h3><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">At Shiftbase, we build workforce software that helps people get work done. Thousands of teams across Europe rely on our platform every day to plan work, track time, and manage leave, freeing them from unnecessary admin so they can focus on what matters and what sparked their business.</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">As we continue to grow in customers, usage and product ambition, the demands on our platform grow with us. Our backend needs to scale in </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">quality, reliability and speed of change</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">. That’s why we’re investing heavily in modernising our platform, building a foundation that allows us to move faster, deliver better experiences, and support the next phase of Shiftbase’s growth.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">About the role:</span></h3><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317"><br>As a Senior Backend Engineer, you are a key driver of both product delivery and platform modernisation. You work on the core of our backend, improving reliability, performance and scalability, with the explicit goal of turning Shiftbase from a platform people enjoy into a platform they love.</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">You help evolve a mature monolithic codebase into a more modular, testable and future-proof architecture. By modernising the foundation of the product, you directly enable better user experiences, faster iteration and higher overall product quality.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">What you'll do</span></h3><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Drive technical excellence</span></strong></p><ul class="ak-ul"><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Design and deliver high-quality, scalable solutions for complex features and system components</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Make informed architectural decisions that balance pragmatism with long-term vision</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Set the bar for technical craft through your contributions and code reviews</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Own complex technical initiatives from design through production, breaking them into testable increments</span></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Build for reliability and scale</span></strong></p><ul class="ak-ul"><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Define comprehensive testing strategies for complex features, championing quality within the team</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Debug and resolve complex issues across multiple components, improving system observability</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Apply security best practices throughout the development lifecycle</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Contribute to monitoring, alerting and system health improvements</span></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Enable team growth</span></strong></p><ul class="ak-ul"><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Mentor engineers with targeted technical guidance and feedback</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Support onboarding and enable a collaborative, knowledge-sharing environment</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Help shape delivery practices and improve team velocity through data-informed decisions</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <h3 style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">What we're looking for</span></h3><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Core technical expertise</span></strong></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">You have deep backend engineering experience with complex, high-scale systems. We don't expect expertise in everything listed below. We value engineers who've built depth and breadth through genuine curiosity and a drive to solve real problems. These are examples of competencies that matter in this role:</span></p><ul class="ak-ul"><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Modern PHP &amp; architectural patterns</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: Experience with hexagonal architecture, domain-driven design, or similar patterns that emphasize domain modeling over framework magic. You can build maintainable systems without relying on framework shortcuts.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">SQL &amp; database design</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: Comfort writing raw SQL (not just ORM abstractions) and working with complex relational schemas particularly around time-sensitive data like scheduling, timesheets and payroll where integrity and performance are critical.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Legacy modernisation experience</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: You've gradually evolved mature systems rather than pursuing big-bang rewrites. You know when to modernize strategically vs. leaving working code untouched, and understand the balance between progress and stability when serving thousands of customers.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Monolith to services</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: Experience breaking down monoliths with good judgment about when distribution solves real problems (deployment bottlenecks, team autonomy) vs. when it adds unnecessary complexity.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Testing in legacy contexts</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: Practical experience with unit and integration testing, particularly incrementally improving coverage in existing systems.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">This might be your dream job if…</span></h3><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">✅ You enjoy </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">modernising a mature platform</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> and turning legacy code into something you’re proud of</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">✅ You get energy from </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">breaking down a monolith</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> and shaping a more modular, service-oriented architecture</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">✅ You care about </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">product quality</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">, not just “shipping code”.</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">✅ You like improving reliability, performance and developer experience as much as adding new features</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">✅ You enjoy working closely with product and frontend to make better technical and product decisions</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">This probably isn’t your dream job if…</span></h3><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">⛔️ You only want to work on </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">greenfield projects</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> and avoid legacy systems altogether</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">⛔️ You’re uncomfortable refactoring existing code or making incremental improvements</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">⛔️ You prefer being handed fully-defined solutions rather than helping shape them</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">⛔️ You’re looking for a role where architecture decisions are already “done”</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">⛔️ You’d rather optimise locally than care about the </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">end-to-end product experience</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><em>Note: Candidates outside the Netherlands will not be considered</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/shiftbase-bv/senior-php-backend-developer-zoetermeer-85077","tags":["IT / Engineering"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Zoetermeer, Zuid-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1793946683},{"slug":"wo-stage-onderzoek-milieukosten-mbv-bestaande-afval-en-emissiestatistieken-den-haag-201330","company_name":"Centraal Bureau voor de Statistiek","title":"wo-stage onderzoek milieukosten m.b.v. bestaande afval- en emissiestatistieken","description":"<h4 style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">wo-</span><span style="color:#0580A1">afstudeerstage/praktijkstage, </span><span style="color:#271D6C">vanaf februari 2027</span></span></strong></h4><p><em><span style="font-size:1.2em">Ben jij die nieuwsgierige onderzoeker die energie krijgt van data, duurzaamheid en nieuwe inzichten?<br>Wil jij een inhoudelijke bijdrage leveren aan de statistieken van het CBS?</span></em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit is jouw </span><span style="color:#0580A1">uitdaging</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Het kabinet wil dat Nederland in 2050 volledig circulair is. Om te kunnen volgen of we die doelstelling halen, is betrouwbare informatie nodig over onder andere afval en emissies naar water. Het CBS verzamelt en publiceert deze gegevens voor bedrijven. Daarbij maken we vooral gebruik van gegevens uit het elektronisch Milieujaarverslag (e-MJV), aangevuld met enquêtes.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Naast de hoeveelheid afval en wateremissies brengen we ook de milieukosten van bedrijven in kaart, bijvoorbeeld de kosten voor afvalverwerking en voor het lozen van afvalwater. Hiervoor wordt nu een aparte enquête gebruikt. Maar is dat eigenlijk wel nodig?</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Tijdens je stage onderzoek je of we de milieukosten voor afval en wateremissies kunnen berekenen met gegevens die al beschikbaar zijn. Je combineert bijvoorbeeld gegevens over de hoeveelheid afval en geloosd water met bestaande indicatoren, zoals gemiddelde kosten per ton afval en sectorspecifieke kosten per kubieke meter geloosd water.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je gaat onder andere:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">bestaande data en indicatoren analyseren en beoordelen op bruikbaarheid;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">onderzoeken welke methode het meest geschikt is om de milieukosten te schatten;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">een berekening of model ontwikkelen waarmee de kosten kunnen worden afgeleid;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">de uitkomsten vergelijken met de beschikbare gegevens uit de huidige enquête;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">onderzoeken hoe betrouwbaar en bruikbaar de schattingen zijn;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">je bevindingen vertalen naar een concreet advies voor het CBS.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Met jouw onderzoek willen we bepalen of we meer uit bestaande data kunnen halen en minder hoeven uit te vragen bij bedrijven. Als blijkt dat de milieukosten betrouwbaar kunnen worden berekend, kunnen de uitkomsten bovendien worden gebruikt om de bestaande afval- en waterstatistieken te controleren.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">In het meest gunstige scenario kan de aparte enquête naar milieukosten gedeeltelijk of helemaal vervallen. Dat betekent minder administratieve lasten voor bedrijven, efficiënter gebruik van beschikbare data en mogelijk betrouwbaardere statistieken.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit is jouw </span><span style="color:#0580A1">stageplek </span><span style="color:#271D6C">bij CBS </span><span style="color:#0580A1">Den Haag</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">We verwelkomen je binnen de sector Leefomgeving bij team Milieu. Met 20 gedreven professionals werken we aan milieu gerelateerde statistieken en doen we onderzoek naar actuele thema’s zoals klimaat(verandering) en circulaire economie. We werken nauw samen met andere teams binnen het CBS.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">We werken hard aan het continu verbeteren van onze statistieken en de cijfers beschikbaar te stellen voor het publiek. Voorbeelden van recente publicaties uit ons team zijn:</span></p><ul><li><p><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.cbs.nl/nl-nl/nieuws/2026/02/bedrijven-investeerden-in-2024-minder-in-milieu"><span style="font-size:1.2em">Bedrijven investeerden in 2024 minder in milieu | CBS</span></a></p></li><li><p><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.cbs.nl/nl-nl/nieuws/2022/50/bijna-2-procent-meer-bedrijfs-en-industrieafval-in-2021"><span style="font-size:1.2em">Bijna 2 procent meer bedrijfs- en industrieafval in 2021 | CBS</span></a></p></li><li><p><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://opendata.cbs.nl/#/CBS/nl/dataset/82863NED/table?dl=E7F90"><span style="font-size:1.2em">Milieukosten en -investeringen van bedrijven | CBS</span></a></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit breng </span><span style="color:#0580A1">jij</span><span style="color:#271D6C"> mee</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je volgt een wo-opleiding milieukunde, economie, technische bestuurskunde, data science of een aanverwante opleiding.</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je hebt affiniteit met het onderwerp circulaire economie.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je bent&nbsp;analytisch sterk en kunt complexe vraagstukken gestructureerd onderzoeken en vertalen naar heldere inzichten.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je kunt goed programmeren in R.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je bent sociaal en communicatief vaardig en kunt je ideeën en bevindingen helder overbrengen aan verschillende gesprekspartners.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Omdat tijdens de stage alle communicatie – zowel mondeling als schriftelijk – in het Nederlands plaatsvindt, is een goede beheersing van de Nederlandse taal noodzakelijk.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit kun je van </span><span style="color:#0580A1">ons</span><span style="color:#271D6C"> verwachten</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Een fijne leeromgeving waarin je:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">jouw competenties in kwantitatieve data-analyse versterkt door gebruik te maken van milieustatistieken en economische databronnen;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">jouw onderzoeksvaardigheden aanscherpt op het gebied van de circulaire economie en levenscyclusanalyse;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">jouw programmeervaardigheden in R verder ontwikkelt;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">ervaring opdoet met het interpreteren van verschillende datasets om betrouwbare profielen op te stellen.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Voor jouw inzet ontvang je een stagevergoeding van € 800 bruto per maand (op basis van 40 uur per week).</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Samen met je stagebegeleider stem je af hoe je hybride kunt werken, met flexibele werktijden en de optie om deels vanuit huis aan jouw stageopdracht te werken.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit zijn </span><span style="color:#0580A1">onze</span><span style="color:#271D6C"> voorwaarden</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Het betreft een stageopdracht en geen werkervaringsplek. Voordat je aan de stage begint verwachten we dat je vanuit de onderwijsinstelling een stagebegeleider hebt, waarmee de stage is afgestemd en concrete leerdoelen zijn afgesproken. <br>Deze stageopdracht is bedoeld voor studenten die momenteel staan ingeschreven bij een onderwijsinstelling; afgestudeerden komen niet in aanmerking.</span></p> <br> <p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/centraal-bureau-voor-de-statistiek/wo-stage-onderzoek-milieukosten-mbv-bestaande-afval-en-emissiestatistieken-den-haag-201330","tags":["Afstudeerstage"],"job_types":["Student college","internship"],"location":"Den Haag, Zuid-Holland, Nederland","created_at":1793946683},{"slug":"wo-stage-woningmarkt-onderzoek-verhuisketens-doorstroom-en-ouderenwoningen-den-haag-321241","company_name":"Centraal Bureau voor de Statistiek","title":"wo-stage woningmarkt onderzoek: verhuisketens, doorstroom en ouderenwoningen","description":"<h4 style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">wo-</span><span style="color:#0580A1">afstudeerstage, </span><span style="color:#271D6C">vanaf februari 2027</span></span></strong></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Ben jij die analytische wo-student die nieuwsgierig is naar de doorstroom op de woningmarkt?<br>Krijg je energie van onderzoek doen, werken met data en programmeren in R?<br>Wil je jouw onderzoeksvaardigheden inzetten voor een actueel maatschappelijk vraagstuk?</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit is jouw </span><span style="color:#0580A1">uitdaging</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Verhuisketens geven inzicht in de doorstroom op de woningmarkt en zijn daardoor actueel en relevant. Het CBS heeft een methode ontwikkeld om deze ketens in beeld te brengen. Het dashboard </span><em><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://dashboards.cbs.nl/verhuisketens/"><span style="font-size:1.2em">Verhuisketens in Nederland</span></a></em><span style="font-size:1.2em"> toont onder meer de gemiddelde lengte van een verhuisketen. Er is echter nog veel ruimte voor verdieping.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Tijdens deze stage kun je afstudeeronderzoek doen naar de rol van ouderenwoningen in de doorstroom op de huizenmarkt. Je kunt daarin op zoek gaan naar antwoorden op de volgende vragen:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">In hoeverre draagt het bouwen van ouderenwoningen bij aan de doorstroom op de woningmarkt?</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Wat is de invloed van vergrijzing en overlijden van ouderen op de doorstroom en het woningaanbod?</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Heb je zelf een goede onderzoeksvraag die aansluit bij dit thema, dan is daar ook ruimte voor.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit is jouw </span><span style="color:#0580A1">stageplek </span><span style="color:#271D6C">bij CBS </span><span style="color:#0580A1">Den Haag</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#292A2E">De afdeling Beleidsstatistiek bestaat uit 70 collega’s verdeeld over Den Haag en Heerlen. Er werken onderzoekers en projectleiders met veel verschillende studieachtergronden binnen onze afdeling. Wij stellen cijfers samen die gebruikt worden voor het ontwikkelen, monitoren en verbeteren van beleid, vaak met een thema-overstijgend karakter. We zijn samenwerkingspartner op het gebied van data-gedreven werken bij overheden.</span></span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit breng </span><span style="color:#0580A1">jij</span><span style="color:#271D6C"> mee</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je bent bijna klaar met jouw wo master-opleiding in de sociale wetenschappen, demografie, ruimtelijke ordening of een aanverwante opleiding en zoekt een afstudeerstage om je opleiding succesvol af te ronden.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Daarnaast:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">heb je (enige) ervaring met programmeren in R;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">kun je zelfstandig onderzoek uitvoeren en uitkomsten analyseren;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">weet je hoe je met verschillende methoden en technieken onderzoek doet.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Kernwoorden die jou omschrijven zijn enthousiast, proactief en analytisch.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Omdat alle communicatie tijdens de stage – zowel mondeling als schriftelijk – in het Nederlands plaatsvindt, is een goede beheersing van de Nederlandse taal noodzakelijk.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit kun je van </span><span style="color:#0580A1">ons</span><span style="color:#271D6C"> verwachten</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Een fijne leeromgeving waarin je:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">jouw vakkennis vergroot en werkervaring opdoet;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">programmeervaardigheden toepast in de praktijk;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">leert werken met CBS-data.<br></span></p></li></ul><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Voor jouw inzet ontvang je een stagevergoeding van € 800 bruto per maand (op basis van 40 uur per week).</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Samen met je stagebegeleider stem je af hoe je hybride kunt werken, met flexibele werktijden en de optie om deels vanuit huis aan jouw stageopdracht te werken.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit zijn </span><span style="color:#0580A1">onze</span><span style="color:#271D6C"> voorwaarden</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Het betreft een stageopdracht en geen werkervaringsplek. Voordat je aan de stage begint verwachten we dat je vanuit de onderwijsinstelling een stagebegeleider hebt, waarmee de stage is afgestemd en concrete leerdoelen zijn afgesproken. <br>Deze stageopdracht is bedoeld voor studenten die momenteel staan ingeschreven bij een onderwijsinstelling; afgestudeerden komen niet in aanmerking.</span></p> <br> <p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/centraal-bureau-voor-de-statistiek/wo-stage-woningmarkt-onderzoek-verhuisketens-doorstroom-en-ouderenwoningen-den-haag-321241","tags":["Afstudeerstage"],"job_types":["Student college","internship"],"location":"Den Haag, Zuid-Holland, Nederland","created_at":1793946683},{"slug":"hbo-stage-social-media-content-creatie-den-haag-116363","company_name":"Centraal Bureau voor de Statistiek","title":"hbo-stage Social Media & Content Creatie","description":"<h4 style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">hbo-</span><span style="color:#0580A1">praktijkstage, </span><span style="color:#271D6C">vanaf februari 2027</span></span></strong></h4><p><em><span style="font-size:1.2em">Ben jij creatief, nieuwsgierig en krijg je energie van social media die écht impact maakt?<br>Grijp de kans om jouw ideeën tot leven te brengen en zichtbaar te maken voor een groot publiek.</span></em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit is jouw </span><span style="color:#0580A1">uitdaging</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Tijdens jouw stage bij het CBS duik je in de wereld van social media en ga je actief bijdragen aan het zichtbaar en begrijpelijk maken van belangrijke maatschappelijke cijfers.<br>Je krijgt de kans om jouw creativiteit in te zetten en verder te ontwikkelen. Je bedenkt nieuwe formats, werkt bestaande concepten uit en vertaalt complexe informatie naar content die mensen echt bereikt. Samen met het socialmediateam werk je aan sterke, herkenbare en aansprekende content.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Dit is wat je gaat doen:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je ontwikkelt creatieve socialmediaformats die aansluiten bij de doelgroep en strategie van het CBS.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je maakt content die daadwerkelijk wordt gepubliceerd op de socialmediakanalen van het CBS. Daarmee lever je een directe bijdrage aan de communicatie van een maatschappelijke organisatie.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je vertaalt statistische informatie naar heldere en toegankelijke verhalen voor een breed publiek.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je denkt actief mee over hoe het CBS zich creatief en onderscheidend kan positioneren op social media.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je draagt bij aan content die impact heeft: jouw werk wordt gezien door een groot publiek en helpt mensen Nederland en de cijfers beter te begrijpen.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit is jouw </span><span style="color:#0580A1">stageplek </span><span style="color:#271D6C">bij CBS </span><span style="color:#0580A1">Den Haag</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je komt terecht in het socialmediateam van het CBS: een klein, hecht team waarin we in een informele sfeer samenwerken. De lijnen zijn kort en er is volop ruimte om ideeën te delen en initiatief te nemen. <br>We zijn continu op zoek naar manieren om onze content beter, creatiever en relevanter te maken. Dat betekent dat we graag experimenteren met formats, inspelen op trends en openstaan voor frisse perspectieven.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit breng </span><span style="color:#0580A1">jij</span><span style="color:#271D6C"> mee</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je volgt een creatieve hbo-opleiding, zoals Communication &amp; Multimedia Design, Creative Business of een vergelijkbare opleiding.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je hebt kennis van en wellicht ervaring met:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Canva;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Adobe Creative Cloud;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">het monteren van short-formcontent;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">de nieuwste trends op social media.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je denkt in mogelijkheden en krijgt energie van samenwerken.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je hebt een ondernemende instelling en komt met innovatieve ideeën.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit kun je van </span><span style="color:#0580A1">ons</span><span style="color:#271D6C"> verwachten</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Een fijne leeromgeving waarin je:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">jouw creatieve en socialmediaskills verder ontwikkelt in een professionele en informele werkomgeving;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">leert om complexe statistische informatie te vertalen naar begrijpelijke en toegankelijke content voor een breed publiek;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">effectief samenwerkt met betrokken collega's in een professioneel team.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Voor jouw inzet ontvang je een stagevergoeding van € 800,- bruto per maand (op basis van 40 uur per week).</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Samen met je stagebegeleider stem je af hoe je hybride kunt werken, met flexibele werktijden en de optie om deels vanuit huis aan jouw stageopdracht te werken.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit zijn </span><span style="color:#0580A1">onze</span><span style="color:#271D6C"> voorwaarden</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Het betreft een stageopdracht en geen werkervaringsplek. Voordat je aan de stage begint verwachten we dat je vanuit de onderwijsinstelling een stagebegeleider hebt, waarmee de stage is afgestemd en concrete leerdoelen zijn afgesproken. <br>Deze stageopdracht is bedoeld voor studenten die momenteel staan ingeschreven bij een onderwijsinstelling; afgestudeerden komen niet in aanmerking.</span></p> <br> <p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/centraal-bureau-voor-de-statistiek/hbo-stage-social-media-content-creatie-den-haag-116363","tags":["Praktijkstage"],"job_types":["Student college","internship"],"location":"Den Haag, Zuid-Holland, Nederland","created_at":1793946683},{"slug":"engineering-manager-mammography-amsterdam-rotterdam-272036","company_name":"DeepHealth","title":"Engineering Manager, Mammography","description":"<p style="text-align:start;">Job Summary</p><p style="text-align:start;">The Engineering Manager, Mammography leads the engineering team behind Mammo Dx, DeepHealth's FDA- and CE-cleared breast cancer detection AI for 2D mammography and 3D tomosynthesis, within the Clinical AI organization that brings together engineering, AI, clinical, and regulatory teams across the US and Europe. The role also acts as Technical Delivery Manager for the team, owning delivery of every release from plan to production. Working with the Mammo product lead, QRC, and US teams, the Engineering Manager, Mammography ensures the right software reaches the right sites on time, with the quality a medical device requires. The role reports to the Software Engineering Manager, Clinical AI Devices.</p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Essential Duties and Responsibilities</p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Team Leadership &amp; Development</p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;">Lead and mentor a team of 3 to 4 engineers; support their technical and professional growth.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Set clear goals, run regular 1:1s and performance reviews, and give constructive feedback.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Recruit, onboard and retain great engineers.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Foster a culture of ownership, quality and continuous improvement.</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Release &amp; Delivery Management (TDM)</p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;">Own the Mammo release plan jointly with the product lead: scope, sizing, milestones and monthly release tracking.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Drive each release end to end: planning, development, verification, regulatory sign-off, deployment and post-release follow-up.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Align the Mammo team's delivery practices, processes and tools with the Clinical AI standards.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Make sure test setups are ready so product can run functional validation on time.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Contribute to the 3- and 6-month roadmap rituals and keep delivery commitments predictable.</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Quality &amp; Regulatory Compliance</p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;">Work with QRC on regulatory impact assessments for every change.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;">Cross-Functional &amp; US Collaboration</p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;">Communicate status, risks and trade-offs clearly to both technical and non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Coordinate with platform, AI and data teams on dependencies.</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Technical Leadership</p><p style="text-align:start;">Take part in design and architecture reviews, challenge estimates and unblock the team.</p><p style="text-align:start;">Keep a strong grasp of the system without writing production code day to day.</p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">PLEASE NOTE: This is not an exhaustive list of all duties, responsibilities and requirements of the position described above. Other functions may be assigned and management retains the right to add or change duties at any time.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p style="text-align:start;">Minimum Qualifications, Education and Experience</p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;">Bachelor's or master's degree in computer science, engineering or a related field, or equivalent experience (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">6+ years in software engineering, with a solid technical background (backend, cloud or data-heavy systems) (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">2+ years managing engineering teams (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Proven track record delivering software releases end to end: planning, QA, deployment and support (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Experience running delivery in a structured environment (regulated industry, enterprise B2B or on-premise deployments) (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Good understanding of modern engineering practices: CI/CD, cloud environments (AWS or GCP), containerized deployments (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">The right to work in France or the Netherlands (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Strong communication and leadership skills, with a focus on team collaboration and ownership (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Ability to mentor and organize a team of senior engineers (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Strong problem-solving and analytical skills (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Structured and reliable: people can count on plans and follow-up (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Comfortable working remotely, asynchronously, and across European and US time zones (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Fluent in English (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Preferred: Experience in medical device software (strong plus).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Preferred: Knowledge of DICOM and radiology workflows (PACS, RIS, modalities, HL7).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"> Preferred: Experience with radiology AI, ideally mammography.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"> Preferred: Experience working with US-based teams and stakeholders.</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Quality Standards</p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#7a7e8d">Communicates, cooperates, and consistently functions professionally and harmoniously with all levels of supervision, co-workers, visitors, and vendors.</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#7a7e8d">Demonstrates initiative, personal awareness, professionalism and integrity, and exercises confidentiality in all areas of performance.· · Follows all local, regional and country laws concerning employment.</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#7a7e8d">Follows all DeepHealth policies and procedures.</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#7a7e8d">Follows data privacy, compliance, safety and confidentiality standards at all times.</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#7a7e8d">Practices universal safety precautions.</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#7a7e8d">Promotes good public relations on the phone and in person.</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#7a7e8d">Adapts and is willing to learn new tasks, methods, and systems.</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#7a7e8d">Reports to work regularly as scheduled; consistently punctual with respect to working hours, meal and rest breaks, and maintains satisfactory personal attendance in accordance with DeepHealth guidelines.</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#7a7e8d">Completes job responsibilities in a quality and timely manner.</span></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Travel</p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;">This position requires domestic and international travel up to 10%, mainly to the US and within Europe.</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Working Environment</p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;">Remote, based in France or the Netherlands. Regular collaboration with US teams requires afternoon overlap with US time zones.</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Physical Demands</p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;">The employee must be able to perform the essential duties and responsibilities of the position, with or without reasonable accommodation.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Salary:</p><p>Paris: 60,000-80,000 EURO</p><p>Netherlands: 70,000-90,000 EURO</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/deephealth/engineering-manager-mammography-amsterdam-rotterdam-272036","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Amsterdam / Rotterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1793946683},{"slug":"strategy-operations-lead-data-intelligence-amsterdam-12335","company_name":"Gresb","title":"Strategy & Operations Lead, Data & Intelligence","description":"<p>GRESB is the global sustainability intelligence standard for real assets. For over 15 years, real estate and infrastructure managers have reported to us, building a dataset of 150,000+ assets across more than 2,000 portfolios. Together with Asset Impact, which tracks emissions for over 300,000 physical assets and 77,000 companies, we’re turning that data into decision-grade intelligence for investors, lenders, index providers and regulators.</p><p>We’re building a new Client &amp; Data Intelligence organization to showcase the value of the data to investors and develop new use cases within the ecosystem. It brings sales, product and data teams together under one leader, the Chief Client &amp; Data Intelligence Officer. This role is the person who makes that organization run. The role is based out of Amsterdam.</p><p><strong>The Role</strong></p><p>You’ll work directly with the Chief Client &amp; Data Intelligence Officer as the strategist and operator at the center of a newly formed team. Your job is to keep decisions moving, teams connected and priority work getting finished, so the leadership team can focus on clients and growth.</p><p>It’s a role for someone who can shape a problem and then see it through. One week you might be building the business case for a new data product; the next you’re tightening the sales pipeline, preparing a board update and unblocking a delivery issue between product and engineering. You’ll move between sales enablement, product and data operations, and you’ll be trusted to run several projects at once without dropping any of them.</p><p>You’ll see the whole business, from client conversations to product decisions to the CEO’s agenda, and you’ll have influence over how a new organization works.</p><p><strong>What you will do</strong></p><p><em>Strategy and priority projects</em></p><ul><li>Lead the organization’s highest-priority initiatives end to end, for example pricing, our investor program, entry into new markets and maturing the data strategy</li><li>Frame the problem, build the analysis, align stakeholders and drive the work through to a decision and implementation</li><li>Bring a recommendation, not just options</li></ul><p><em>Operating rhythm and decision-making</em></p><ul><li>Run the team’s operating cadence: weekly deal desk, fortnightly product council and monthly business review</li><li>Own the decision log, so it’s always clear what was decided, by whom and what happens next</li><li>Spot blockers between sales, product and data teams early and clear them</li></ul><p><em>Commercial operations and sales enablement</em></p><ul><li>Own pricing and support deal structuring with the sales team</li><li>Keep pipeline and ARR reporting accurate and trusted, with one view across GRESB</li><li>Work with sales and product to make sure the team has what it needs to showcase the value of the data products</li></ul><p><em>Reporting and communication</em></p><ul><li>Build and run the monthly CEO dashboard and KPI reporting</li><li>Prepare senior leadership, board and client materials that are clear, concise and decision-ready</li><li>Act as the Chief Client &amp; Data Intelligence Officer’s point of contact when they’re away</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>What success looks like</strong></p><p>In your first six months</p><ul><li>The operating rhythm is running and people rely on it</li><li>The decision log is live and used</li><li>There’s one trusted ARR view across GRESB data products</li></ul><p>By the end of your first year</p><ul><li>At least two priority projects have been taken from problem to implemented decision</li><li>Leadership and board reporting runs on a predictable monthly cycle with little rework</li><li>Sales, product and data teams describe fewer handoff issues, and escalations get resolved faster</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Around 6–10 years of experience</li><li>A grounding in top-tier management consulting or Big Four advisory, in strategy, sustainability, data or technology</li><li>Ideally, spent time at a sustainability data, ESG ratings, real asset or financial data business</li><li>Strong business acumen and ability to work well in a cross-functional, global environment.</li><li>Experience implementing AI or advanced analytics solutions within a commercial or sales environment.</li><li>Proficiency in CRM, data analytics, and visualization tools.</li><li>A working understanding of how data products are packaged, priced and sold</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>How you work</strong></p><ul><li>You think in structure: you can break down an ambiguous problem, find what matters and build a clear path forward</li><li>You finish things. You run several projects at once and see each one through to the end</li><li>You’re organized, detail-oriented and work well in systems</li><li>You write and present clearly, whether it’s a one-page update or a board deck</li><li>You get things done without formal authority, by earning trust across sales, product and engineering</li><li>You’re comfortable moving between the big picture and the detail in the same day</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul><li>Involvement in a fast growing international data-driven company</li><li>Opportunity to work with a highly talented and committed team in a supportive environment with strong camaraderie</li><li>Annual leave of 25 days per calendar year</li><li>2 volunteering days off per year</li><li>Company pension plan</li><li>Free public transport to and from the Amsterdam office</li><li>Free and healthy office lunch catered daily&nbsp;</li><li>Annual professional development budget</li><li>Home office budget&nbsp;</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>About GRESB</strong></p><p>GRESB is the global sustainability intelligence standard for real assets. We transform sustainability data into decision-grade intelligence that drives capital allocation and asset improvement.</p><p><strong>Our vision:&nbsp;</strong>An investment industry that plays a central role in creating a sustainable world.</p><p><strong>Our mission:</strong>&nbsp;To provide financial markets with actionable sustainability insights, data, and benchmarks. More than 100 global institutional and financial investors rely on GRESB to help guide their investment decisions, mitigating risk, improving portfolio quality, and driving long-term financial success.</p><p>The GRESB team is an energetic group of more than 100 individuals from diverse backgrounds with experience spanning sustainability, data science, software development, real estate, infrastructure, and the capital markets. Most of us work out of our head office in Amsterdam or one of our satellite offices in London, Paris, Berlin, Boston, Singapore, or Sydney. We’re passionate about tackling the sustainability challenge by providing the insights that will power the markets of the future and enable investors to allocate the world’s capital in a more responsible way.</p><p>GRESB is a portfolio company of BeyondNetZero, General Atlantic's climate investing platform.</p><p>GRESB is an equitable, diverse, and inclusive workplace, one at which all workers - regardless of their gender, race, ethnicity, national origin, age, sexual orientation, identity, education, or disability - feel valued and respected. We are committed to a non-discriminatory approach to hiring and provide equal opportunity for employment and advancement in all of our teams and programs.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/gresb/strategy-operations-lead-data-intelligence-amsterdam-12335","tags":["Commercial Real Estate","Business development"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam, Netherlands","created_at":1793938810}],"links":{"first":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/api/job-board-api?page=1","last":null,"prev":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/api/job-board-api?page=1","next":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/api/job-board-api?page=3"},"meta":{"current_page":2,"current_page_url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/api/job-board-api?page=2","from":101,"path":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/api/job-board-api","per_page":300,"to":300,"terms":"This is a free public API for jobs, please do not abuse. I would appreciate linking back to the site. By using the API, you agree to the terms of service present on Arbeitnow.com","info":"Jobs are updated every hour and order by the `created_at` timestamp. Use `?page=` to paginate. Read more information here: https://www.arbeitnow.com/blog/job-board-api"}}
